== checking it ==
  holding 42 once one is added
  holding nothing
== leaving early ==
  {7, 3, 12, 5} -> 24
  {7, 3, 5}     -> 0
== every way through ==
  95 -> excellent
  61 -> a pass
  12 -> not yet
== where it stops ==
  from a branch: 0
  from a loop:   20
  from a try:    30
== what a closure takes away ==
  before: 7
  after:  0
  the copy is empty too, and reads as a plain value inside a check
== writing one out ==
  a fallback, printed:   0
  a fallback, joined:    0
  a fallback, in a hole: 0
  proven, printed:       41
  proven, joined:        41
  proven, in a hole:     41
== comparing them ==
  41 and 41:            true
  41 and nothing:       false
  nothing and nothing:  true
  41 and 7:             false
  41 and plain 41:      true
  nothing and plain 41: false
